---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PrinterGuide from '../../components/PrinterGuide.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="No-Subscription Printer Evidence Guide"
  description="A practical guide to printers that do not require mandatory ink subscriptions, with notes on refillable tanks, toner, Linux support, and lock-in risk."
>
  <div class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--amber);">Buyer guide</p>
    <h1>Four no-subscription printer options, checked against official documents.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      “Subscription optional” is only one part of ownership. This guide also checks ordinary supplies, local connections, account boundaries, support material, and what the manufacturer does not promise.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section" id="quick-comparison">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--amber);">Quick comparison</p><h2>Start with the job you need to do</h2></div>
        <p>These are four different options, not an overall ranking. Hardware and supply details below summarize the July 22, 2026 reviews; Linux download evidence was added on September 18. Account-free setup has not been verified for any of the four.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions" aria-label="Choose a printing need">
        <a class="button" href="#brother-hl-l2460dw">Black-and-white documents</a>
        <a class="button" href="#epson-ecotank-et-2850">Refillable color + duplex</a>
        <a class="button" href="#brother-mfc-j4335dw">Color + document feeder</a>
        <a class="button" href="/guides/linux-compatible-printers/">Linux printing or scanning</a>
      </div>
      <p class="evidence-note">On smaller screens, scroll the comparison sideways. Each model links to its detailed evidence and official sources below.</p>
      <div class="comparison-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Printer comparison" tabindex="0">
        <table>
          <caption>Compare functions and supplies before reading the full reviews.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / use</th><th scope="col">Output</th><th scope="col">Scan / feeder</th><th scope="col">Automatic two-sided printing</th><th scope="col">Ordinary supplies</th><th scope="col">Account-free setup</th><th scope="col">Main limit</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#brother-hl-l2460dw">Brother HL-L2460DW</a><br />Text documents</th><td>Black-and-white laser</td><td>No scanner</td><td>Yes</td><td>TN830-family toner; separate DR830 drum</td><td>Not verified</td><td>No color or copying</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#epson-ecotank-et-2850">Epson ET-2850</a><br />Refillable color with duplex</th><td>Color inkjet</td><td>Flatbed; no ADF</td><td>Yes</td><td>Refill bottles</td><td>Not verified</td><td>Check the suffix: ET-2850U has different subscription requirements</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#canon-pixma-g3270">Canon G3270</a><br />Refillable color with dual-band Wi-Fi</th><td>Color inkjet</td><td>Flatbed; no ADF</td><td>No</td><td>GI-21 bottles</td><td>Not verified</td><td>No automatic duplex or Ethernet</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><a href="#brother-mfc-j4335dw">Brother MFC-J4335DW</a><br />Color office documents</th><td>Color inkjet</td><td>Scanner and ADF; do not assume duplex scanning</td><td>Yes</td><td>LC406 retail cartridges</td><td>Not verified</td><td>Cartridges rather than refill bottles; no Ethernet</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><a href="#accounts-and-offline-use">Need no account or no internet?</a> · <a href="#occasional-printing">Only print occasionally?</a> · <a href="/guides/print-after-cancelling-hp-instant-ink/">Already cancelling Instant Ink?</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--amber);">Sourced model reviews</p>
          <h2>Different strengths, different limits</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The full U.S. model reviews date from July 22, 2026; the MFC-J4335DW Linux download correction was checked September 18. Other model fields have not been reverified for this update. These are document reviews, not independent product tests.</p>
      </div>
      <PrinterGuide />
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="article">
    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>Why buyers worry about subscriptions and accounts</h2>
      <p>
        A low purchase price can hide a supply plan, a cloud-connected replenishment service, or cartridges that change behavior after cancellation. A printer may offer an optional plan while its normal retail supplies remain usable; another model variant may require an active plan. The exact model suffix and the type of cartridge or bottle matter more than a general “subscription-ready” label.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>USB, local network, mobile apps, and cloud printing are not the same</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>USB</strong> is a direct computer-to-printer path. It reduces network dependence, but the setup software may still request an account.</li>
        <li><strong>Local network printing</strong> uses Wi-Fi or Ethernet on your own network. IPP, AirPrint, Mopria, and LPR/LPD can support local jobs without sending the document through a vendor cloud.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile apps</strong> can be convenient for setup, scanning, and maintenance, but their account and telemetry requirements should be checked separately.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloud printing</strong> enables remote jobs or scan-to-cloud features and normally adds an account, internet connection, and service-policy dependency.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="article-section" id="accounts-and-offline-use">
      <h2>Can I use these printers without an account or internet?</h2>
      <p>We have not verified account-free first-time setup for these four models. Their reviewed documentation lists local connections, but that alone does not prove that setup, scanning, or maintenance never asks for an account.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>MFC-J4335DW:</strong> USB and Wi-Fi Direct are documented. Account-free setup and every scan workflow remain untested.</li>
        <li><strong>ET-2850:</strong> the standard model documents USB and Wi-Fi Direct; optional Epson Connect cloud services are a separate path. Do not apply these notes to ET-2850U.</li>
        <li><strong>G3270:</strong> USB and Wireless Direct are documented. ARS replenishment capability does not establish its account-free setup behavior.</li>
        <li><strong>HL-L2460DW:</strong> USB, Ethernet, and local network protocols are documented. It has no scanner; account-free setup has not been tested here.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Before buying, ask the manufacturer about your exact OS and connection: “Can I complete first-time setup and print locally without creating a vendor account? Does scanning require one? Which functions stop if internet access is unavailable?” Check the answers against the setup manual, and test your required workflow during the return period. Use the model-specific sources in the reviews above.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="article-section" id="occasional-printing">
      <h2>What if I print only a few times a month?</h2>
      <p>Start by deciding whether you actually need color and scanning. If your jobs are black-and-white documents, compare the HL-L2460DW with the cost of a separate scanner if needed. If color matters, compare the two refillable models and the MFC-J4335DW, then read the exact model’s storage and maintenance instructions before choosing.</p>
      <p>Do not choose on bottle or cartridge price alone. Include the purchase price, replacement supplies, a separate drum where applicable, maintenance, and the functions you would otherwise buy separately. This guide has no current price survey or tested cost-per-page comparison, so it does not claim a cheapest option or promise an idle period with no maintenance.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>How the ownership checks work</h2>
      <p>
        Every model receives the same six evidence checks: subscription choice, basic use without a subscription, consumable transparency, local connection, long-term support material, and documentation completeness. “Documented” means a reviewed official source directly supports the point. “Mixed” means the useful path is documented but an important boundary remains unclear. “Not documented” would mean we found no adequate official support. We do not add these labels into a score or rank models by invented precision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>Reusable pre-purchase checklist</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Match the full model number and suffix on the box, retailer listing, support page, and manual.</li>
        <li>Find the ordinary cartridge, toner, drum, or bottle part numbers before considering a subscription offer.</li>
        <li>Read the cancellation terms: do plan cartridges stop working, and what must replace them?</li>
        <li>Confirm at least one local path you can actually use: USB, Ethernet, Wi-Fi Direct, IPP, AirPrint, Mopria, or CUPS.</li>
        <li>Check whether first-time setup, scanning, or maintenance requires an app or vendor account.</li>
        <li>Open the current OS support page for your exact operating system and architecture.</li>
        <li>Read the current warranty and return policy for your region; do not assume a U.S. term applies elsewhere.</li>
        <li>Treat third-party supply compatibility as unknown unless the manufacturer documents it. Firmware, consumables, and policies can change after this page's verification date.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  #quick-comparison,
  #accounts-and-offline-use,
  #occasional-printing,
  :global(.printer-card) {
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    #quick-comparison,
    #accounts-and-offline-use,
    #occasional-printing,
    :global(.printer-card) {
      scroll-margin-top: 160px;
    }
  }
</style>
